{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788049928043587278,"compiled_state":{"alias":"citreous-anorthite-dormouse","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"e6d887d0d3cc02d119e5955dc5433a5141ff3ba56f6c4a340ab5263aa6d864a0","event_uuid":"7b67e870-af80-48e6-b736-72e89c462f2f","position":{"commit_sha":"8b84a8b5ef7e6043ca045616259a7bc95031c10b","position":"1788047880492577718-7b67e870-af80-48e6-b736-72e89c462f2f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"392396fea6cc3f7448dce6424c80c4ca0e689a0d05d9598896c00a429d4b1ba6","event_uuid":"751eeb88-a95b-4469-9c6e-bcff628c34cd","position":{"commit_sha":"ff7ce81700e1dd0575faf384ac486f6098579778","position":"1788047893748535432-751eeb88-a95b-4469-9c6e-bcff628c34cd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788047880492577718,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"751eeb88-a95b-4469-9c6e-bcff628c34cd","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1c0d-fe83-0254-444a"}],"description":"While rotating /rebar/prod/anthropic-api-key and re-materializing the container .env, a manual `docker compose up -d --force-recreate review-bot opcert mcp` on i-00880b2c7f13527c5 RACED the `rebar-autodeploy.timer` (which runs `docker compose` every ~2 min). The concurrent compose runs produced `Error response from daemon: No such container: <id>` and the manual `up` aborted partway, transiently leaving review-bot/opcert/mcp created-but-not-started (only gerrit up) — a self-inflicted ~1-2 min outage of the code-review bot, op-cert gate, and MCP server.\n\nRecovery that worked: `systemctl disable --now rebar-autodeploy.timer` → `docker compose up -d` → verify ps + `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` length in each consumer → `systemctl enable --now rebar-autodeploy.timer`.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md secret-rotation / targeted-restart section documents the autodeploy-timer race and prescribes pausing `rebar-autodeploy.timer` for the recreate window (disable --now → up -d → re-enable --now), OR an equivalent lock so a manual compose op and the autodeploy tick cannot run concurrently.\n- The `docker compose up -d --force-recreate <svc>` examples in that runbook cross-reference the pause step.\n\nNon-goals: changing autodeploy's cadence or adding a compose-level lock in autodeploy.sh itself (a heavier design change — file separately if wanted). This is a documentation/procedure fix.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ops","runbook","review-bot","mcp","autodeploy"],"ticket_id":"fd5d-cd3d-871e-4c51","ticket_type":"task","title":"Document autodeploy-race hazard in review-bot-ops secret-rotation procedure","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7b67e870-af80-48e6-b736-72e89c462f2f","751eeb88-a95b-4469-9c6e-bcff628c34cd"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788049928043587278,"uuid":"77081913-9918-49ca-abff-7b5ae40c4cd4"}